      "writtenOn": "2025-05-21T16:25:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Coverity (a static analyzer) warns about potential signed integer overflow in lines 2373, 2381, 2384, 2385. I will use line 2385 as an example.\n\nIt says:\n\n\u003e CID 523775: (#1 of 1): Unintentional integer overflow (OVERFLOW_BEFORE_WIDEN)\noverflow_before_widen: Potentially overflowing expression count_intrabc * kBlockArea * 30 with type int (32 bits, signed) is evaluated using 32-bit arithmetic, and then used in a context that expects an expression of type int64_t const (64 bits, signed).\n\nand suggests\n\n\u003e To avoid overflow, cast either count_intrabc * kBlockArea or 30 to type int64_t const.\n\nI think `count_intrabc * kBlockArea * 30` can potentially overflow an `int` (I am not certain because of the complicated if statements around the `++count_intrabc` statements), so it is safer to cast `count_intrabc` to `int64_t` as Coverity suggested.\n\nIf you agree, I can take care of adding the `int64_t` casts.",
      "revId": "88a775af3a0a1cb7b82db1c1f64f56712b565566",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    }
